Takauji ASHIKAGA was a busho ( Japanese military commander ) from the late Kamakura period to the period of the Northern and Southern Courts ( Japan ) .
He was the first Seii Taishogun ( literally , `` great general who subdues the barbarians '' ) of the Muromachi bakufu ( Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun ) .
His real family name was Genji ( Minamoto clan ) .
He was born as the legitimate son of Sadachika ASHIKAGA , who was a distinguished family of Kawachi-Genji ( Minamoto clan ) .
At first , he was given a portion of his name from Takatoki HOJO , the regent , and called himself Takauji .
When Emperor Godaigo raised an army at Mt. <unk> in Hoki Province in Genko , he led the bakufu army as a powerful gokenin ( an immediate vassal of the shogunate in the Kamakura and Muromachi through Edo periods ) , but he raised an army of <unk> at <unk> Shrine in Tanba Province , and destroyed Rokuhara Tandai ( an administrative and judicial agency in Rokuhara , Kyoto ) .
He was regarded as the first achievement of the fall of the bakufu , and was given one character of the real name of Emperor Godaigo 's imina ( personal name ) , <unk> , and changed his name to Takauji .
While Godaigo 's Kenmu Restoration lost its support , he left the east and suppressed the Nakasendai War , and showed his own political power in Kamakura .
Due to this , the relationship with the Imperial Court became worse , and he temporarily fled to Mt. Hiei due to Godaigo 's counterattack , but he escaped to Kyushu temporarily due to the counterattack by Godaigo .
He went to Kyoto again from Kyushu , and was appointed as Seii Taishogun by the retired Emperor Kogon and Emperor Komyo , and established a new samurai government ( the Muromachi bakufu [ Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun ] ) .
Godaigo moved to Yoshino and founded the Southern Court ( Japan ) .
After the establishment of the bakufu , he established two politics with his younger brother Tadayoshi ASHIKAGA , but later opposed Tadayoshi and developed into the Kanno Disturbance .
The war ended after the death of Tadayoshi , but continued to suppress the <unk> power such as the Southern Court and made efforts to stabilize the rule .
